  "notes": [
    "carBox: eyeballed on a ruler over the pack photo; segModel birefnet-general (the lite model followed the blister on the other cars)",
    "carBox/wheels/mask.remove (photo px, traced on 2-4x ruler crops with a green-paint threshold): birefnet took in the blister bubble hugging the car - a band above the roof, the gap between wing and rear deck, the haze over the bonnet and the blister wall left of the tail. One remove polygon cuts everything above the car's real top line (wing plate y~2759 x 318-462 with its wide side upright down to the deck at y~2879, rear screen slope to the roof at y 2761 x 780-1120, A-pillar and bonnet/fender line down to the nose top ~(1918, 3005)) and left of the tail bumper (x<294). Wheel circles are the tyres (rear c(615,3145) r120, front c(1600,3150) r123); auto-detect had found the rims only. carBox tightened to the measured extent",
    "model.glass.remove (sheet px, glass.jpg on a 2x ruler): the automatic finder took the two black roof stripes on the top view for glass (one cyan block from rear window to windscreen) and the tops of the tyres; cut out so the stripes are paint, not cabin seen through glass",
    "model.rebake.glass: side/left left out - Tripo modelled the side windows as open holes (the sheet masks put glass tint on the seats seen through them). Top traced on the mesh (trace-top.png, Tripo's dark window paint + clay panel edges): the aligned top drawing puts the rear window ~35 px rearward of the mesh's panel (x 205-338) and over the deck, and its mask had taken in the roof stripes. Front traced on the windscreen panel (the sheet mask rose to y 1204 over the black roof stripe ends and dipped below the cowl). Rear traced on the panel between pillar edges and around the wing uprights (upright-hidden glass comes from the top view), leaving out the black diagonal C-pillar edges. All three traced on one half and mirrored",
    "model.rebake.noalign [top]: Tripo never saw the top and the aligned top drawing came out stepped (bonnet stripes broken into offset blocks by the vents, match 0.04-0.19); projected straight the stripes and J-Liu TH graphic sit straight on the bonnet and roof",
    "model.rebake.skip top x 126-208 (rear deck between wing uprights and rear window): the top drawing's rear window sits ~35 px rearward of the mesh's, so it painted dark glass-with-cabin onto the deck; the deck keeps Tripo's green. trust top x 58-126 (wing uprights' top faces): Tripo had painted them white, the drawing's green wins",
    "model.rebake.trust + flat rear (sheet px 718-836 x 1285-1326, NISSAN emblem and GT-R badge): Tripo's own emblem relief and garbled GT-R paint sat beside the drawn badges and doubled them; the drawing wins there and Tripo's relief is flattened",
    "model.rebake.glass rear traced on both sides (not mirrored): mirroring left the car's left outboard pane opaque and put tint on the right wing upright",
    "paint: the ChatGPT sheet draws the green Spectraflame with a swirly engraved/etched pattern that the real toy doesn't have (it is smooth gloss); the repaint carries that texture over from the drawings - left as is, flagged for the founder"
  ],
